<meta name="description" content="Choosing where to live can be a major headache if you do not know the area: the procedures may not be the same as you are used to, and the information will be in a language you may not understand. In an ideal world you would visit the area a month or so before moving to select your new home. But this may not be possible, so you might need to stay in a hotel or short-stay facility initially." />
